/** @mainpage Qore imagemagick Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section imagemagickintro ImageMagick Module Introduction

    The \c imagemagick module provides comprehensive image processing and manipulation capabilities
    for %Qore by wrapping the ImageMagick MagickWand C API. It supports over 200 image formats and
    offers a wide range of operations including:

    - Image I/O: read and write images from files or in-memory binary data
    - Format conversion: convert between PNG, JPEG, GIF, BMP, TIFF, WebP, and many other formats
    - Resizing: multiple algorithms including Lanczos, Mitchell, and bilinear filtering
    - Cropping, trimming, and canvas manipulation
    - Transformations: rotation, flipping, shearing, deskewing, auto-orientation
    - Blur and sharpen: Gaussian, adaptive, unsharp mask, motion blur, and more
    - Color adjustments: brightness, contrast, gamma, levels, modulate, normalize
    - Artistic effects: charcoal, sepia, oil paint, edge detection, emboss, and more
    - Compositing: overlay images with various blending operators
    - Drawing: vector shapes, text annotations, and custom drawing operations
    - Metadata: read/write EXIF, ICC profiles, and image properties
    - Multi-image support: animated GIF frames, multi-page TIFF

    To use this module, use the \c %%requires directive as follows:
    @code{.py}
%requires imagemagick
    @endcode

    This module provides the following classes:
    - @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage "MagickImage": the main image class for loading,
      manipulating, and saving images
    - @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickDrawing "MagickDrawing": vector graphics drawing class for
      shapes and text

    And the following hashdecls:
    - @ref Qore::ImageMagick::ImageInfo "ImageInfo": image metadata
    - @ref Qore::ImageMagick::ImageResolutionInfo "ImageResolutionInfo": image resolution (DPI)
    - @ref Qore::ImageMagick::PointInfo "PointInfo": x/y coordinate pair

    @section imagemagickreq ImageMagick Module Requirements

    This module requires:
    - %Qore 2.0+
    - ImageMagick 7.0+ with MagickWand development libraries
      - Ubuntu/Debian: \c libmagickwand-dev
      - Alpine: \c imagemagick-dev
      - Fedora/RHEL: \c ImageMagick-devel

    @section imagemagickquickstart Quick Start

    @subsection imagemagick_loading Loading and Saving Images

    @par Loading from file:
    @code{.py}
%requires imagemagick

# Load from file
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Load from binary data
binary data = ReadOnlyFile::readBinaryFile("photo.png");
MagickImage img2(data);

# Load with explicit format
MagickImage img3(raw_data, "RGB");

# Create a blank canvas
MagickImage canvas(800, 600, "white");
    @endcode

    @par Saving images:
    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Save to file (format inferred from extension)
img.writeFile("/path/to/output.png");

# Get as binary data
binary png_data = img.toData();

# Get as binary data in a specific format
binary jpeg_data = img.toData("JPEG");
binary webp_data = img.toData("WEBP");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_info Getting Image Information

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Individual properties
printf("Dimensions: %dx%d\n", img.width(), img.height());
printf("Format: %s, Depth: %d-bit\n", img.format(), img.depth());
printf("Colorspace: %s\n", img.colorspace());
printf("Type: %s\n", img.imageType());

# Resolution
hash<ImageResolutionInfo> res = img.resolution();
printf("Resolution: %.0fx%.0f DPI\n", res.x, res.y);

# Signature
printf("Signature: %s\n", img.signature());

# All info at once
hash<ImageInfo> info = img.getInfo();
printf("Colors: %d, Images: %d\n", info.colors, info.number_images);

# Identify string (detailed ImageMagick report)
printf("%s\n", img.identify());
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_metadata Reading EXIF and Metadata

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Get specific EXIF properties
*string camera = img.getProperty("exif:Make");
*string model = img.getProperty("exif:Model");
*string date = img.getProperty("exif:DateTimeOriginal");

# List all EXIF properties
hash<auto> exif = img.getProperties("exif:*");
map printf("%s: %s\n", $1.key, $1.value), exif.pairIterator();

# Get ICC profile
*binary icc = img.getProfile("icc");

# Set a custom property
img.setProperty("comment", "Processed by Qore");

# Strip all metadata (for privacy)
img.strip();
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_resize Resizing Images

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Simple resize with default Lanczos filter
img.resize(800, 600);

# Resize with explicit filter
img.resize(1920, 1080, "Lanczos");

# Create thumbnail (fast, optimized for small sizes)
MagickImage thumb = img.copy();
thumb.thumbnail(150, 150);

# Scale (fast, simple algorithm)
MagickImage scaled = img.copy();
scaled.scale(400, 300);

# Adaptive resize (good for small changes)
MagickImage adaptive = img.copy();
adaptive.adaptiveResize(750, 500);

# Sample (nearest neighbor, very fast)
MagickImage sampled = img.copy();
sampled.sample(200, 150);

# Resample (change DPI)
MagickImage resampled = img.copy();
resampled.resample(300.0, 300.0, "Lanczos");

# Liquid rescale (content-aware resizing)
MagickImage liquid = img.copy();
liquid.liquidRescale(600, 400);

img.writeFile("/path/to/resized.jpg");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_crop Cropping and Trimming

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Crop a 300x200 region starting at (50, 100)
img.crop(300, 200, 50, 100);

# Trim whitespace borders
MagickImage img2("/path/to/scanned.png");
img2.trim(10.0);  # fuzz factor for near-white

# Extend canvas with padding
MagickImage img3("/path/to/logo.png");
img3.extent(1000, 800, -100, -50);

# Shave pixels from edges
MagickImage img4("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img4.shave(20, 20);  # remove 20px from each side
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_transform Rotation, Flipping, and Orientation

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Rotate 90 degrees clockwise
img.rotate(90.0);

# Rotate 45 degrees with colored background
MagickImage img2("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img2.rotate(45.0, "transparent");

# Mirror horizontally (left-right)
MagickImage img3("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img3.flop();

# Mirror vertically (top-bottom)
MagickImage img4("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img4.flip();

# Transpose (rotate 90 + flip)
MagickImage img5("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img5.transpose();

# Shear
MagickImage img6("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img6.shear(10.0, 0.0);

# Auto-orient based on EXIF orientation tag
MagickImage photo("/path/to/camera-photo.jpg");
photo.autoOrient();
photo.writeFile("/path/to/oriented.jpg");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_blur Blur and Sharpen

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Gaussian blur (radius=0 auto-selects, sigma controls strength)
img.gaussianBlur(0.0, 3.0);

# Simple blur
MagickImage img2("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img2.blur(0.0, 2.0);

# Sharpen
MagickImage sharp("/path/to/photo.jpg");
sharp.sharpen(0.0, 1.5);

# Unsharp mask (common for print preparation)
MagickImage print_img("/path/to/photo.jpg");
print_img.unsharpMask(0.0, 1.0, 1.5, 0.05);

# Motion blur at 45-degree angle
MagickImage motion("/path/to/photo.jpg");
motion.motionBlur(0.0, 12.0, 45.0);

# Adaptive blur (preserves edges)
MagickImage adaptive("/path/to/photo.jpg");
adaptive.adaptiveBlur(0.0, 2.0);

# Adaptive sharpen (sharpens details without amplifying noise)
MagickImage asharp("/path/to/photo.jpg");
asharp.adaptiveSharpen(0.0, 1.5);

# Rotational blur
MagickImage rotblur("/path/to/photo.jpg");
rotblur.rotationalBlur(5.0);
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_color Color Adjustments

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Adjust brightness (+20%) and contrast (+10%)
img.brightnessContrast(20.0, 10.0);

# Gamma correction
MagickImage img2("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img2.gamma(1.2);

# Levels adjustment (black point, gamma, white point)
MagickImage img3("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img3.level(10.0, 1.0, 90.0);

# Adjust hue/saturation/lightness via modulate
# (brightness%, saturation%, hue-rotation)
MagickImage img4("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img4.modulate(100.0, 130.0, 100.0);  # boost saturation 30%

# Auto-enhance
MagickImage dark("/path/to/dark-photo.jpg");
dark.autoLevel();
dark.autoGamma();

# Normalize (stretch histogram to full range)
MagickImage img5("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img5.normalize();

# Equalize histogram
MagickImage img6("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img6.equalize();

# Invert colors
MagickImage img7("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img7.negate();

# Sigmoidal contrast (more subtle than brightnessContrast)
MagickImage img8("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img8.sigmoidalContrast(True, 3.0, 50.0);

# White balance
MagickImage img9("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img9.whiteBalance();

# Transform colorspace
MagickImage img10("/path/to/photo.jpg");
img10.transformColorspace("Gray");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_effects Artistic Effects

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Charcoal drawing effect
MagickImage charcoal = img.copy();
charcoal.charcoal(1.0, 0.5);
charcoal.writeFile("charcoal.png");

# Sepia tone (vintage look)
MagickImage sepia = img.copy();
sepia.sepiaTone(80.0);
sepia.writeFile("sepia.jpg");

# Oil painting effect
MagickImage oil = img.copy();
oil.oilPaint(4.0);
oil.writeFile("oil-paint.jpg");

# Edge detection
MagickImage edges = img.copy();
edges.edge(2.0);
edges.writeFile("edges.png");

# Emboss (3D relief effect)
MagickImage embossed = img.copy();
embossed.emboss(0.0, 1.5);
embossed.writeFile("embossed.jpg");

# Vignette (darkened edges)
MagickImage vignette = img.copy();
vignette.vignette(0.0, 10.0, 20, 20);
vignette.writeFile("vignette.jpg");

# Swirl distortion
MagickImage swirl = img.copy();
swirl.swirl(90.0);
swirl.writeFile("swirl.jpg");

# Wave distortion
MagickImage wave = img.copy();
wave.wave(5.0, 50.0);
wave.writeFile("wave.jpg");

# Posterize (reduce color palette)
MagickImage poster = img.copy();
poster.posterize(4);
poster.writeFile("posterized.png");

# Sketch effect
MagickImage sketch = img.copy();
sketch.sketch(0.0, 10.0, 45.0);
sketch.writeFile("sketch.jpg");

# Solarize
MagickImage solar = img.copy();
solar.solarize(50.0);
solar.writeFile("solarized.jpg");

# Add noise
MagickImage noisy = img.copy();
noisy.addNoise("Gaussian", 0.5);
noisy.writeFile("noisy.jpg");

# Reduce noise / denoise
MagickImage denoised = img.copy();
denoised.waveletDenoise(10.0);
denoised.writeFile("denoised.jpg");

# Despeckle
MagickImage despeckled = img.copy();
despeckled.despeckle();
despeckled.writeFile("despeckled.jpg");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_composite Compositing (Watermarks and Overlays)

    @code{.py}
# Add a watermark overlay
MagickImage photo("/path/to/photo.jpg");
MagickImage watermark("/path/to/watermark.png");

# Composite at specific position
photo.composite(watermark, "Over", 50, 50);

# Or use gravity for automatic positioning
MagickImage photo2("/path/to/photo.jpg");
photo2.compositeGravity(watermark, "Over", "SouthEast");
photo2.writeFile("watermarked.jpg");

# Multiply blend (darkroom effect)
MagickImage base("/path/to/base.jpg");
MagickImage texture("/path/to/texture.jpg");
base.composite(texture, "Multiply", 0, 0);
base.writeFile("blended.jpg");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_drawing Drawing Shapes and Text

    @code{.py}
# Create a blank canvas and draw on it
MagickImage canvas(800, 600, "white");
MagickDrawing draw();

# Draw a red rectangle
draw.setFillColor("red");
draw.setStrokeColor("black");
draw.setStrokeWidth(2.0);
draw.rectangle(50.0, 50.0, 200.0, 150.0);

# Draw a blue circle
draw.setFillColor("blue");
draw.circle(400.0, 300.0, 400.0, 200.0);

# Draw a rounded rectangle
draw.setFillColor("green");
draw.roundRectangle(500.0, 50.0, 700.0, 200.0, 15.0, 15.0);

# Draw a line
draw.setStrokeColor("purple");
draw.setStrokeWidth(3.0);
draw.line(50.0, 400.0, 750.0, 400.0);

# Add text
draw.setFillColor("black");
draw.setFontSize(36.0);
draw.annotation(300.0, 500.0, "Hello, World!");

# Apply drawing to canvas
canvas.draw(draw);
canvas.writeFile("drawing.png");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_annotate Adding Text Annotations to Photos

    @code{.py}
MagickImage photo("/path/to/photo.jpg");

# Simple annotation
photo.annotate("Copyright 2026", 10.0, float(photo.height()) - 20.0, 0.0,
    "Arial", 14.0, "white", "gray");
photo.writeFile("annotated.jpg");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_convert Format Conversion with Quality Control

    @code{.py}
# PNG to JPEG with quality setting
MagickImage img("/path/to/image.png");
img.setFormat("JPEG");
img.setCompressionQuality(85);
img.writeFile("/path/to/output.jpg");

# Get binary data in a specific format
binary webp_data = img.toData("WEBP");
binary tiff_data = img.toData("TIFF");
binary bmp_data = img.toData("BMP");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_inmemory In-Memory Processing (Web Service Pattern)

    @code{.py}
# Process image received as binary data (e.g., from HTTP request)
binary input_data = get_image_from_request();
MagickImage img(input_data);

# Resize for web
img.resize(800, 600, "Lanczos");
img.setCompressionQuality(80);
img.strip();  # remove metadata for privacy

# Return as JPEG binary
binary output = img.toData("JPEG");
send_response(output, "image/jpeg");
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_multiframe Working with Multi-Frame Images

    @code{.py}
# Read animated GIF
MagickImage gif("/path/to/animated.gif");
printf("Frames: %d\n", gif.numberImages());

# Navigate frames
gif.resetIterator();
int i = 0;
while (gif.hasNextImage()) {
    gif.nextImage();
    printf("Frame %d: %dx%d\n", i++, gif.width(), gif.height());
}

# Jump to a specific frame
gif.setIteratorIndex(3);
printf("Frame 3 index: %d\n", gif.iteratorIndex());
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_batch Batch Processing

    @code{.py}
%requires imagemagick

# Process all JPEGs in a directory
list<string> files = glob("/path/to/photos/*.jpg");
foreach string file in (files) {
    MagickImage img(file);
    img.autoOrient();
    img.resize(1920, 1080, "Lanczos");
    img.setCompressionQuality(85);
    img.strip();
    string outfile = regex_subst(file, "\\.jpg$", "_web.jpg");
    img.writeFile(outfile);
    printf("Processed: %s -> %s\n", file, outfile);
}
    @endcode

    @subsection imagemagick_pixel Pixel Access

    @code{.py}
MagickImage img(100, 100, "white");

# Set individual pixel colors
img.setPixelColor(50, 50, "red");
img.setPixelColor(51, 50, "green");
img.setPixelColor(52, 50, "blue");

# Read pixel color
string color = img.getPixelColor(50, 50);
printf("Pixel color: %s\n", color);  # e.g., "srgb(255,0,0)"
    @endcode

    @section imagemagickformats Supported Image Formats

    ImageMagick supports over 200 image formats. The most commonly used formats include:

    | Format | Read | Write | Description |
    |--------|------|-------|-------------|
    | PNG | Yes | Yes | Portable Network Graphics (lossless, supports transparency) |
    | JPEG | Yes | Yes | Joint Photographic Experts Group (lossy, good for photos) |
    | GIF | Yes | Yes | Graphics Interchange Format (256 colors, supports animation) |
    | BMP | Yes | Yes | Windows Bitmap (uncompressed) |
    | TIFF | Yes | Yes | Tagged Image File Format (high quality, supports layers) |
    | WebP | Yes | Yes | Google WebP (good lossy and lossless compression) |
    | SVG | Yes | Yes | Scalable Vector Graphics |
    | PDF | Yes | Yes | Portable Document Format |
    | ICO | Yes | Yes | Windows Icon format |
    | PSD | Yes | No | Adobe Photoshop Document |
    | EXR | Yes | Yes | OpenEXR (HDR imaging) |

    The available formats depend on your ImageMagick installation and its configured delegates.

    @section imagemagickfilters Filter Types

    The following filter types are available for resize operations via
    @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::resize() "MagickImage::resize()" and
    @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::resample() "MagickImage::resample()":

    | Constant | Filter | Description | Best For |
    |----------|--------|-------------|----------|
    | \c IM_FILTER_LANCZOS | Lanczos | High quality sinc-windowed filter | General purpose (default) |
    | \c IM_FILTER_MITCHELL | Mitchell | Balanced sharpness and ringing | Photo downscaling |
    | \c IM_FILTER_CATROM | Catrom | Catmull-Rom spline interpolation | Image reduction |
    | \c IM_FILTER_GAUSSIAN | Gaussian | Gaussian curve smoothing | Smooth scaling |
    | \c IM_FILTER_BOX | Box | Nearest neighbor averaging | Pixel art upscaling |
    | \c IM_FILTER_TRIANGLE | Triangle | Bilinear interpolation | Fast moderate quality |
    | \c IM_FILTER_POINT | Point | Nearest neighbor (no interpolation) | Fastest, pixel-perfect |
    | \c IM_FILTER_CUBIC | Cubic | Cubic interpolation | General purpose |

    @section imagemagickcolorspaces Colorspaces

    Supported colorspaces for
    @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::transformColorspace() "MagickImage::transformColorspace()":

    | Colorspace | Description |
    |------------|-------------|
    | sRGB | Standard RGB (default for web) |
    | RGB | Linear RGB |
    | CMYK | Cyan, Magenta, Yellow, Key (print) |
    | Gray | Grayscale |
    | HSL | Hue, Saturation, Lightness |
    | HSV | Hue, Saturation, Value |
    | Lab | CIE L*a*b* (perceptual) |
    | LCH | Lightness, Chroma, Hue |
    | YCbCr | Luminance + Chrominance (video) |
    | Transparent | Transparent colorspace |

    @section imagemagickcomposite Composite Operators

    Available blending operators for
    @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::composite() "MagickImage::composite()" and
    @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::compositeGravity() "MagickImage::compositeGravity()":

    | Operator | Description |
    |----------|-------------|
    | Over | Standard overlay (respects alpha channel) |
    | Multiply | Multiply blend (darkening, like darkroom double exposure) |
    | Screen | Screen blend (lightening effect) |
    | Overlay | Overlay blend (contrast enhancement) |
    | Add | Additive blend |
    | Difference | Absolute difference of colors |
    | Dissolve | Dissolve blend |
    | HardLight | Hard light blend |
    | SoftLight | Soft light blend |
    | ColorBurn | Color burn blend |
    | ColorDodge | Color dodge blend |
    | Exclusion | Exclusion blend |

    @section imagemagickgravity Gravity Types

    Gravity types for positioning in
    @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::compositeGravity() "MagickImage::compositeGravity()":

    | Gravity | Position |
    |---------|----------|
    | NorthWest | Top-left corner |
    | North | Top center |
    | NorthEast | Top-right corner |
    | West | Center left |
    | Center | Center of image |
    | East | Center right |
    | SouthWest | Bottom-left corner |
    | South | Bottom center |
    | SouthEast | Bottom-right corner |

    @section imagemagicknoise Noise Types

    Noise types for @ref Qore::ImageMagick::MagickImage::addNoise() "MagickImage::addNoise()":

    | Noise Type | Description |
    |------------|-------------|
    | Uniform | Uniform random noise |
    | Gaussian | Gaussian (normal distribution) noise |
    | Multiplicative | Multiplicative Gaussian noise |
    | Impulse | Impulse (salt and pepper) noise |
    | Laplacian | Laplacian noise |
    | Poisson | Poisson noise |

    @section imagemagickdataprovider Data Provider API

    The \c ImageMagickDataProvider module provides integration with the %Qore data provider
    framework for use with Qorus. It registers the \c "imagemagick" factory with the following
    provider tree:

    @code
    imagemagick{}/
      image/                        # Container: image operations
        resize                      # Resize with filter selection
        crop                        # Crop to region
        rotate                      # Rotate by angle
        flip                        # Flip/mirror
        blur                        # Gaussian blur
        sharpen                     # Sharpen
        brightness-contrast         # Adjust brightness and contrast
        composite                   # Overlay images
        annotate                    # Add text
        thumbnail                   # Fast thumbnail creation
        auto-orient                 # Fix EXIF orientation
        strip                       # Remove metadata
        effects/                    # Container: artistic effects
          charcoal                  # Charcoal drawing
          sepia                     # Sepia tone
          oil-paint                 # Oil painting
          edge                      # Edge detection
          emboss                    # 3D emboss
      convert/                      # Container: format operations
        format                      # Convert image format
      info/                         # Container: information
        get                         # Get image metadata
    @endcode

    All image operations accept either \c input_path (file path) or \c data (binary) as input,
    with an optional \c output_format to control the output format. All return binary \c data
    plus \c width, \c height, \c format, and \c size metadata.

    @par Using Data Provider to Resize:
    @code{.py}
%requires ImageMagickDataProvider

AbstractDataProvider dp = DataProvider::getFactoryObjectFromStringEx("imagemagick{}/image/resize");
hash<auto> result = dp.doRequest({
    "data": input_binary,
    "width": 800,
    "height": 600,
    "filter": "Lanczos",
    "output_format": "JPEG",
});
binary resized = result.data;
printf("Output: %dx%d %s (%d bytes)\n", result.width, result.height, result.format, result.size);
    @endcode

    @par Using Data Provider to Get Image Info:
    @code{.py}
AbstractDataProvider dp = DataProvider::getFactoryObjectFromStringEx("imagemagick{}/info/get");
hash<auto> info = dp.doRequest({"data": image_binary});
printf("Format: %s, Size: %dx%d, Colors: %d\n", info.format, info.width, info.height, info.colors);
    @endcode

    @section imagemagickerrors Error Handling

    All errors are raised as \c IMAGEMAGICK-ERROR exceptions with descriptive messages
    from the ImageMagick library.

    @par Error handling example:
    @code{.py}
try {
    MagickImage img("/nonexistent/path.jpg");
} catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
    if (ex.err == "IMAGEMAGICK-ERROR") {
        printf("ImageMagick error: %s\n", ex.desc);
    }
}
    @endcode

    Common error scenarios:
    - Reading a nonexistent or unreadable file
    - Reading corrupt or unsupported image data
    - Writing to an unwritable path
    - Invalid color strings
    - Invalid filter, colorspace, or composite operator names
    - Out-of-bounds pixel coordinates

